Z||000000||nette||04-21-2001||09:56 PM||||First question: the right-side 1/4 window is cracked at the top.  Should I replace this or try and fix it?  Is it easy to remove?<P>Second question: got new emblems for the 1/4 windows. What's the best way to glue them in? (I am assuming they glue in...)<P>Final tidbit: had posted "front end noise" questions last week.  Replaced inner/outer bearings and seal.  Noise is gone!  Thanks for the help on that.<P>------------------<BR>nette<BR>87 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-21-2001||10:24 PM||||When my GT windows were cracked, I had them replaced.<P>If you have new emblems(?), didn't directions come with them for the install?<P>I don't know what kind of emblem you are talking about.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||nette||04-21-2001||11:10 PM||||Sorry, I am talking about the Pontiac arrow-head emblem on the front lower corner of the quarter window.  And there were no instructions with the new emblem. BTW, my car is a notchback.<P>------------------<BR>nette<BR>87 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||04-21-2001||11:30 PM||||nette, a little drop of crazy glue will work just fine........||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||04-22-2001||11:17 AM||||Hey Nette!<BR>first clean out the recess the arrow head fits into...<BR>Also, drill an 1/8th inch hole in the center of the recess (lets out excess epoxy)...<BR>Use 5 minute epoxy to glue it in...<BR>Be sure the glue fills the recess, as it keeps water out...<BR>slowly press the arrow head in, till seated...<BR>If any epoxy comes out the sides, wipe it off while wet with a rag wet with alcohol...<BR>You want to avoid any air pockets where water could get in and freeze, as that is how they pop out...<BR>crash...<p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||04-22-2001||11:23 AM||||Oh ya, almost forgot, go to <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A>  to see some cool replacement sailpanels...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
